# CONCEPT_MASTER — force.pdl
#
# Master z-node record. Schema per A-TEARIT-IS-ALL-YOU-NEED.md §3 and
# AI-TRACK-BRAINSTORM-QUESTIONS.md Q9 §9b (hub-and-spoke Concept Bank).
# A master is a named, abstract concept. Its own N_SLOTS pointer-slots
# let a master point at OTHER masters (concept-to-concept, e.g.
# force -> motion), using the exact same slotted-pointer record shape
# a spoke/word uses to point at masters — one generic record type,
# reused at both levels, per Q9 9b ("few, flexible, growable
# primitives" discipline, not two formats).
#
# On-disk stores only ACTIVE (non-zero) slots — sparse form. A loader
# expands this to the full N_SLOTS-wide record in memory (Q9 9b
# "Compress/decompress"). Slot indices below are stable identifiers
# for this record, not filled in write order.

NODE | force
KIND | master
N_SLOTS | 8

# SLOT | <idx> | POINTS_TO=<other master name> | WEIGHT=<float, -1.0..1.0>
SLOT | 0 | POINTS_TO=motion | WEIGHT=0.70
SLOT | 1 | POINTS_TO=energy | WEIGHT=0.50

# ---- MIRROR TABLE — DERIVED, GENERATED. DO NOT HAND-EDIT. ----
# Regenerated by ops/concept_mirror_rebuild.sh from every spoke's own
# forward record (the spoke's slots are the ONE authoritative copy of
# any weight, per Q9 9b's "weights live in exactly one place"
# resolution). This block is a rebuildable index only — same
# discipline as the phymoji sprite-cache bug Q9 9b cites as the
# failure mode this avoids (two independently-editable copies of the
# same fact). Running concept_mirror_rebuild.sh overwrites everything
MIRROR_GENERATED_AT | 2026-09-22 16:16:19
MIRROR_FROM | gravity_constant | WEIGHT=0.60
